WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.621
Gandhi led three nationwide movements

2
00:00:02.621 --> 00:00:04.278
against British rule.

3
00:00:04.278 --> 00:00:06.158
They came roughly a decade

4
00:00:06.158 --> 00:00:07.139
apart.

5
00:00:07.472 --> 00:00:11.022
Non-Cooperation began in 1920.

6
00:00:11.022 --> 00:00:14.357
Civil Disobedience in 1930.

7
00:00:14.357 --> 00:00:17.590
And Quit India in 1942.

8
00:00:17.936 --> 00:00:20.622
After violence at Chauri Chaura

9
00:00:20.622 --> 00:00:21.517
in 1922,

10
00:00:21.517 --> 00:00:24.583
Gandhi called off Non-Cooperation.

11
00:00:24.583 --> 00:00:26.290
The Salt March to Dandi

12
00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.158
began Civil Disobedience.

13
00:00:28.158 --> 00:00:29.991
And on the eighth of

14
00:00:29.991 --> 00:00:31.980
August 1942 came Do or

15
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:32.903
Die.

16
00:00:33.231 --> 00:00:34.542
In GS1 answers,

17
00:00:34.542 --> 00:00:36.321
show how each one widened

18
00:00:36.321 --> 00:00:37.285
the base.

19
00:00:37.285 --> 00:00:38.372
Peasants, women,

20
00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:39.796
workers, and students,

21
00:00:39.796 --> 00:00:41.422
in growing numbers.

22
00:00:42.107 --> 00:00:43.378
Your turn.

23
00:00:43.378 --> 00:00:46.489
Why was Non-Cooperation called off?
